## Problem classes

### `Local-only hotspot fails with location already granted`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Private network never starts a hotspot. Log shows nearby wifi denied, or `onFailed` with no passphrase | `NEARBY_WIFI_DEVICES` uses `neverForLocation`, so fine location does not cover it, and the runtime permission was never requested. An empty log is not success | Request that permission before `startLocalOnlyHotspot` on API 33+. Log `onFailed` reason, timeout, and missing creds. Do not log the passphrase |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Saved-network lookup does not compile`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Kotlin `Unresolved reference` on a `WifiConfiguration` field such as a hidden flag | The field is not in the app compile SDK | A saved hit is a matching SSID and a non-negative network id. Do not read hidden configuration flags |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Hotspot SSID is random and the joiner never hears it`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `startLocalOnlyHotspot` without a config picks the SSID | Custom config API is missing or was ignored | Read SSID and passphrase from `LocalOnlyHotspotReservation` and send them on the sealed control channel after Accept. Use `startLocalOnlyHotspotWithConfiguration` when that public method exists. |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Host lost its home Wi-Fi for the whole day`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| STA dropped and never returned | Visible switch was treated as "keep hotspot up" | Switch controls BLE only. Tear the reservation down when no client is associated and the idle timer fires, or on Disband. |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `System Settings QR did not yield the password`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| App launched the DPP QR intent and still has no PSK | That intent renders a code for a passphrase the caller already passed in | Do not use it to extract. Show our own QR only after the PSK is known. Extraction is Shizuku or typed entry. |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Specifier with internet never connects`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| LAN join times out; no system picker; `Couldn't reach the device` | `WifiNetworkSpecifier` is local-only. A request that still asks for `INTERNET` is rejected | Remove `INTERNET` for specifier (hotspot / Wi-Fi Direct). For a normal LAN, do not use specifier |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Suggestion Join leaves the current STA`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| User taps the suggestion Join notification and stays on the old SSID | Suggestion saves/approves. A healthy validated STA is not displaced | Privileged connect when Shizuku is ready on the joiner. Else open the system Wi-Fi panel and wait until the current SSID matches |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `App modal hides the system Wi-Fi sheet`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Specifier or Settings panel never appears; taps hit the in-app waiting dialog | Join ran while a Flutter modal still owned the window | Dismiss the waiting UI before the native join. Then specifier, panel, or privileged connect |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Privileged connect snaps back to the previous STA`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Target SSID associates, then the phone returns to the old network within seconds | Network selection prefers the previous validated-internet STA | Known, not pinned yet. Candidate: disable auto-join on the previous network for the session and restore it on leave. Do not leave auto-join off if the process dies |

